  "editorReview": {
    "text": "The book's core strength lies in its materialist approach: the 'Portability Trilemma' is convincingly built from the physical realities of battery chemistry and thermal limits, making engineering compromises tangible. Chapter 18's dissection of the Nintendo Switch exemplifies this, brilliantly capturing its 'software-defined sacrifices.' However, a significant structural flaw undercuts its biographical promise. The fascinating, detail-rich portrait of Gunpei Yokoi in Chapter 1—where his design philosophy grows from observed life—fades away. His later contradictions and failures are left unexam",
